<title>FRANCE: GEC Alsthom wins $61 mln order for trains.</title>
<headline>GEC Alsthom wins $61 mln order for trains.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>GEC Alsthom said on Tuesday it had won an order worth $61 million to supply the Santiago Metro authority in Chile with six 7-car trains for lines one and two.</p>
<p>The order for aluminium, tyre-mounted trains follows delivery of 17 new generation trains for line 5 and will bring the total number supplied to the Santiago metro since 1978 to 438, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>It did not say when the new trains would be supplied.</p>
<p>GEC Alsthom is a 50-50 joint venture between General Electric Co Plc of Britan and France's Alcatel Alsthom.</p>
</text>
